## Core
{%- if is_template %}

### Support for Multiple CI/CD Platforms

- GitHub **Recommended**
    - Creating repos under both users and orgs is supported
- Azure DevOps **Deprecated**
    - See [Azure DevOps Limitations](azure-devops.md) for details about features missing for AzDO, and why this platform is being phased out

### Support for Public (Open-Source) and Private (Closed-Source) Repositories

This template fully supports both public/open-source and private/closed-source repositories. See [`project_visibility`](template-questions.md#project_visibility-public-private) for what differs.

### Support for Existing Projects

Postmodern templates are designed to allow either the creation of new templates from scratch or adoption for existing projects with existing code repos. See [Applying to an Existing Project](../getting-started/existing-project.md).
{%- endif %}

### Support for Template Updates

Keeping projects in sync with their parent template is a core feature of [Copier](https://github.com/copier-org/copier). A scheduled {% if is_template %}GitHub Actions workflow/Azure DevOps pipeline{% elif using_github %}GitHub Actions workflow{% else %}Azure DevOps pipeline{% endif %} checks for new template releases, and `mise run copier-update` applies them. See [Updating from the Parent Template](../maintaining/updating-from-template.md).
{%- if is_template %}

### Support for Child/Recursive Templates

It is highly encouraged for you to take this template and make your own child template that meets your needs. Your child template can (optionally) receive updates from this template. See [Template Projects](#template-projects) and [Extending This Template](../maintaining/extending-the-template.md).
{%- endif %}

